          "source": "",
          "thread": "fiat on/off ramp buildout",
          "why": "MetaMask, Uniswap, Coinbase, Enso, and Stripe all launched or deepened fiat-crypto conversion tools in the same window, signaling an infrastructure race that readers tracking adoption closely followed."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "regulated stablecoin vs fiat rails",
          "why": "frxUSD, UStb, WYST, and Stripe's stablecoin accounts each represent a different model for replacing or replicating fiat settlement onchain, and readers engaged with each as a distinct horse in the stablecoin wars."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "crypto-to-fiat laundering routes",
          "why": "The Lazarus Group's $200M laundering thread and the AML-at-off-ramps piece together revealed how fiat conversion points are the critical vulnerability in crypto compliance, drawing a risk-aware readership."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "exchange fiat access battles",
          "why": "Binance.US losing and fighting to restore USD rails, and Binance losing its EUR Paysafe partner, made clear that banking access is an existential chokepoint exchanges can lose without warning."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "institutional fiat-crypto bridge",
          "why": "Visa, Citi/BVNK, and Swift piloting fiat-tokenization and cross-border digital settlement signaled that TradFi is building its own on-ramp infrastructure rather than ceding ground to crypto-native players."
        }
      ]
